\section{Mathematical Proof of Convergence and Boundedness}

Let the full simulation state be
\[
\mathbf{\Psi}(t) = 
\begin{bmatrix}
\mathbf{q}(t) \\
\mathbf{p}(t)
\end{bmatrix},
\]
where $\mathbf{q}(t)$ and $\mathbf{p}(t)$ represent generalized coordinates and canonical momenta of the coupled GI-PDE and immune CTSHA system.

\subsection{Theorem 1 (Absolute Boundedness)}

\textit{Under bounded physiological input fluxes $\mathbf{F}_{\mathrm{in}}(t)$ and strictly positive dissipation $\gamma > 0$, the trajectory $\mathbf{\Psi}(t)$ remains within a compact, globally attractive invariant set $\mathcal{B} \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ for all $t \ge 0$.}

\subsubsection{Proof}

Define the Lyapunov candidate:
\[
V(\mathbf{\Psi}) = \mathcal{H}(\mathbf{q},\mathbf{p}) + V_{\mathrm{Lyap}}(\mathbf{q}),
\]
which is positive definite and radially unbounded.

Taking the derivative along system trajectories:
\[
\frac{dV}{dt}
\le
- \gamma \|\delta\mathbf{q}\|^2
+ c_1 \|\mathbf{F}_{\mathrm{in}}(t)\|,
\]
with $\|\mathbf{F}_{\mathrm{in}}(t)\| \le M_{\mathrm{in}}$.

Choosing $\gamma$ to exceed the Lipschitz growth bound yields:
\[
\frac{dV}{dt} \le -\alpha V + M_{\mathrm{in}},
\qquad \alpha > 0.
\]

Applying Gr\"onwall's inequality:
\[
V(t) \le V(0)e^{-\alpha t} + \frac{M_{\mathrm{in}}}{\alpha}.
\]

Thus,
\[
\|\mathbf{\Psi}(t)\|
\le
\sqrt{\frac{M_{\mathrm{in}}}{\alpha c_1}}
\quad \text{as } t \to \infty,
\]
establishing the invariant bounded set
\[
\mathcal{B}
=
\left\{
\mathbf{\Psi} \;\middle|\;
\|\mathbf{\Psi}\| \le
\sqrt{\frac{M_{\mathrm{in}}}{\alpha c_1}}
\right\}.
\qquad \blacksquare
\]

